{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"poisonous-flamy-chuckwalla","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\nPass-1 submits every chunk and AGENT future at once into a 6-wide pool (src/rebar/llm/plan_review/pass1.py:438,462-464); with a cold cache the first ~6 concurrent calls each pay a full cache-WRITE for the byte-identical plan-bearing system prefix — measured shape ~7.9N effective plan-tokens versus an ideal 2.15N (~3.7x). The warm-then-fan-out pattern already exists, proven, for container bins (pass1.py:184-232, gated on CACHE_MIN_PREFIX_TOKENS=4096 and >=2 pairings, with graceful degradation on a failed warm).\n\n## Approach\nPort the container warm gate to the main pool: when the estimated shared-prefix tokens >= CACHE_MIN_PREFIX_TOKENS and (chunks + agent criteria) >= 2, run the first single-turn chunk to completion serially (writing the cache prefix), then submit the remainder to the pool; a non-systemic warm failure degrades to direct fan-out exactly as the container path does (pass1.py:203-212). Verification uses the per-call cache metrics landed by the usage-instrumentation story. Alternative rejected: serializing the whole pool — forfeits 6-way parallelism to save only the redundant writes the single warm call already eliminates.\n\n## Scope\nsrc/rebar/llm/plan_review/pass1.py, tests/llm/test_pass1_warmup.py.\n\n## Testing\nUnit with a recording FakeRunner: with the gate met, exactly one call completes before any pool submission and the rest fan out; below the token gate or with a single call, behavior is unchanged; a warm-call exception falls back to direct fan-out and the review completes.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] With >= 2 Pass-1 calls and a large plan, the first call completes before the pool starts (checked: unit test asserting call-ordering via a recording runner).\n- [ ] Small plans and single-call reviews bypass the warm-up (checked: unit test).\n- [ ] A failing warm call degrades to today's direct fan-out and the review still completes (checked: unit test).\n- [ ] In a stubbed-usage run, the shared prefix incurs one cache write and N-1 cache reads (checked: unit test over the per-call usage records from the instrumentation seam).","id":"25fa-0865-8b61-498c","parent_id":"a492-3e46-ca44-40a5","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Warm-then-fan-out for the Pass-1 chunk and agent pool"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785384361946852001,"uuid":"3a0a0b31-dbbe-4df2-beee-a9a057872e5a"}